12.4:
O Lord, my God, to thee will I cry: hear my supplication;
And unto thee will I make confession of my sins,
And unto thee will I reveal my transgressions of thy law.

12.9:
For lo, the wild primaeval Lion pursues me;
And his children are the gods of the Egyptians that I have abandoned and destroyed;
And their father the Devil is trying to devour me.

12.11:
Save me, O Lord, deserted as I am,
For my father and mother denied me,
Because I destroyed and shattered their gods;
And I have no other hope save in thee, O Lord;
For thou art the father of the orphans, and the champion of the persecuted,
And the help of them that are oppressed.

10.16:
The doorkeepers of the place of darkness shall give him their glory and beauty as share;
his kingdom has vanished, his throne has mouldered,
and the honour of his stature is in (Sheol) Hades.

10.17:
For he has loved the beauty of the serpent
and the scales (skins) of the dragon;
his gall and his venom belong to the Northern One (Zphuni = Adder).

10.20:
Righteous is the Lord, and His judgments are true,
with him there is no preference of person;
for He judges all alike.
